  TEST 2: Cloned pane (listeners stripped): 229 SCROLLED ✓
  TEST 3: Wheel scroll: 0 NOT SCROLLED (expected - non-touch)

=== Root Cause ===
TerminalPane.dispose() called this._keyDisposable.dispose() which threw TypeError
because attachCustomKeyEventHandler() returns void, not IDisposable.
The throw aborted dispose() before touch handler cleanup, leaving non-passive
touchmove with preventDefault() on the pane element. When the block renderer
mounted on the same element, the lingering listener blocked native scroll.

=== Fix ===
1. Moved touch handler cleanup to TOP of dispose()
2. this._keyDisposable?.dispose() (optional chaining)

=== Verdict ===
PASS — Block mode touch scroll works (229 SCROLLED)
PASS — Terminal mode not broken (xterm present, touch handler active)
